{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00641",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 10.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "Thanks for seeing us. Darragh has had a cold since Sunday and last night I heard a whistling in his chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.46,
      "end_seconds": 21.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "You were right to bring him. Hello Darragh. Good boy, sit on Mammy's knee. How old is he? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 23.67,
      "end_seconds": 27.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "He's two and a half. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.85,
      "end_seconds": 35.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Tell me about the whistling. Is it there all the time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 37.56,
      "end_seconds": 47.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "It's mostly when he breathes out. It comes and goes. It was loudest at about two this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.08,
      "end_seconds": 50.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Mammy, nose. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 51.22,
      "end_seconds": 55.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "His nose is running, love. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.81,
      "end_seconds": 62.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Is he feeding and drinking normally? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 65.25,
      "end_seconds": 74.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Yes, he's grand in himself. He's still playing, he ate his breakfast, and he's been drinking his milk. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.09,
      "end_seconds": 82.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "And any temperature? Has he felt hot at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 84.1,
      "end_seconds": 90.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "No, I checked him this morning, he's not hot. No temperature at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.65,
      "end_seconds": 105.15,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "That's what I wanted to hear. Let me listen to his chest. Darragh, can I put my stethoscope on your tummy? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.08,
      "end_seconds": 110.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Cold! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.92,
      "end_seconds": 138.95,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "It's cold, isn't it? I'll warm it up for you. Breathe in and out like a doggy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 141.64,
      "end_seconds": 144.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Is he wheezing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.7,
      "end_seconds": 159.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.57,
      "text": "There's a bit of wheeze on both sides when he breathes out, but the air's moving well, there's no work of breathing and no sucking in under the ribs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 160.7,
      "end_seconds": 163.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Oh, that's good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.44,
      "end_seconds": 174.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I'd say this is a viral wheeze, brought on by his cold, which is very common in toddlers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 176.22,
      "end_seconds": 180.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Will he grow out of it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.76,
      "end_seconds": 191.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "Most children do. It tends to be triggered by colds and fade as they get bigger. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 192.71,
      "end_seconds": 201.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Does he need anything for it? I've got a nebuliser at home from my niece. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.99,
      "end_seconds": 214.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "Not today. He doesn't need anything, and I wouldn't use someone else's equipment. We'll see how he gets on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 217.46,
      "end_seconds": 222.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Okay. And what should I do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.17,
      "end_seconds": 236.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "Keep him drinking, let him rest, and keep the room smoke-free. Raise his head a little at night if he'll tolerate a pillow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 238.34,
      "end_seconds": 241.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "He hates pillows. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.41,
      "end_seconds": 246.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Then don't worry about that one. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 248.43,
      "end_seconds": 253.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "And when would I be worried? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.46,
      "end_seconds": 269.78,
      "duration_seconds": 15.32,
      "text": "If he's breathing fast, you can see his tummy sucking in, he can't finish a sentence or a feed, or his lips go a bit blue, call 999."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 272.51,
      "end_seconds": 275.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Oh God. Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.06,
      "end_seconds": 292.35,
      "duration_seconds": 15.29,
      "text": "I don't expect it, but I'd rather you know. And if the wheeze is still there after five days, or he's not feeding, bring him back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 293.83,
      "end_seconds": 296.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Five days, got it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.5,
      "end_seconds": 302.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Well done, Darragh. You were great. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.2,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Bye bye! ~"
    }
  ]
}
